<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Perperna</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Perpenna</span></b> , ae, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman surname.</i> A famous
			person of this name was M. Perperna, <i>the murderer of
				Sertorius</i>, <i>who was defeated by Pompey</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv. 44, 27, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Epit.
				96</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2, 30, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 2,
				20, 6</span></i>.—Form Perpenna, <i><span class="en">Nep. Cat.
				1, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 3, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 36,
				4, 9</span></i>.</div>
